CORE THEORY
Reaction: R-OH + SOCl2 → R-Cl + SO2 + HCl.
Reagent: Thionyl Chloride.

WHY IS IT THE BEST METHOD?
It is considered the most effective way to prepare pure alkyl chlorides because both byproducts (SO2 and HCl) are gases and escape the reaction mixture, leaving behind pure R-Cl.

MECHANISM AND STEREOCHEMISTRY (JEE ADVANCED INSIGHT)
The stereochemical outcome depends on the presence of a base.

- CASE 1: SOCl2 alone (SNi mechanism)
Result: Retention of configuration. The halogen replaces the OH from the same side.
