| Sandmeyer | Cu2X2 / HX | Aryl-X (Cl, Br) | High yield |
| Gattermann | Cu powder / HX | Aryl-X (Cl, Br) | Modified Sandmeyer |
| Balz-Schiemann | HBF4 then Heat | Aryl Fluoride | Specific for R-F |
| KI Reaction | KI + Warmth | Aryl Iodide | No catalyst needed |
| Hunsdiecker | Ag salt + Br2 | Alkyl/Aryl Bromide | Decarboxylation|

7. PROBLEM-SOLVING FRAMEWORK

| Question Type | Identification Clues | Approach / Strategy |
|---------------|----------------------|---------------------|
| Name the reaction | Cu2Cl2 vs Cu powder | Cu2X2 = Sandmeyer; Cu powder = Gattermann. |
| Prepare R-F | Diazonium salt | Use Balz-Schiemann (HBF4 + Heat). |
| Prepare R-I | Diazonium salt | Simply warm with KI solution. |
